extends layout

block content
    .content
        #projects
          h4 Internet of Things Plant Monitor
          p One of the problems that amateur gardeners face is that we're sometimes unsure whether we are watering our plants not enough or too much. As a side project, I installed Internet of Things sensors to track the soil moisture, temperature and humidity of my basil plants.
          
          .row
            .col-md-9.col-sm-3(style='padding-top: 10px')
              h6 Moisture [%]
            .col-md-3.col-sm-9.text-right(style='padding-top: 10px') 7/14/2020-8/24/2020
          iframe(width='100%' height='284' frameborder='0' src='https://observablehq.com/embed/@chichutschang/july-2020-moisture-data?cells=chart')
          
          .row
            .col-md-9.col-sm-3(style='padding-top: 10px')
              h6 Temperature [&#176;F]
            .col-md-3.col-sm-9.text-right(style='padding-top: 10px') 7/14/2020-8/24/2020
          iframe(width='100%' height='284' frameborder='0' src='https://observablehq.com/embed/@chichutschang/july-2020-temperature-data?cells=chart')
          
          h6 Equipment
          .table-responsive
            table.table.table-borderless
              tr
                td(width='40%')
                  ul(style='list-style-type: none;')
                    li 2 Node MCU Amica (ESP 8266 Wi-Fi Module)
                    li 1 VMA 311 Temperature sensor
                    li 1 YL-69 Moisture sensor
                    li 1 Raspberry Pi
                    li 1 LCD panel
                    li 1 LED light
                td
                  img(src='/images/plants1.png' width='100%')
          
          h6 Architecture
          p The architecture for this Internet of Things side project is fairly straightforward. The sensors collect data from the soil and air. The data is sent via Wi-Fi to an Internet gateway, which in this case is the MQTT program running on a Raspberry Pi. The MQTT program sends the data to a MongoDB database in the cloud. This website pulls the data from the cloud and renders the data in the form of graphs.
          img(src='/images/plants2.png' width='100%')
          
          h6 Temperature
          p
            | For the temperature and humidity sensor, I connected a VMA 311 sensor and RGB backlight LCD panel to a 
            u
              a(href='https://www.nodemcu.com/index_en.html') Node MCU Amica
            |  development board with Wi-Fi. This 
            u
              a(href='https://create.arduino.cc/projecthub/ThothLoki/portable-arduino-temp-humidity-sensor-with-lcd-a750f4') Portable Arduino Temp/Humidity Sensor with LCD
            |  tutorial explains how to set up the VMA 311 sensor and LCD panel.
          
