          h6 MQTT
          p
            | Once the sensors are up and running, the data is sent to a MQTT broker. This 
            u
              a(href='https://www.mongodb.com/blog/post/implementing-an-endtoend-iot-solution-in-mongodb-from-sensor-to-cloud') MongoDB blog
            |  explains the architecture. I wrote code in Python using the 
            u
              a(href='https://pypi.org/project/paho-mqtt/') Eclipse Paho MQTT Python Client
            |  to subscribe to messages and publish to MongoDB. Here is the code:
          pre
            != codeSnippet3

          h6 MongoDB
          p In MongoDB, I created a new cluster called "plants" and a database for each plant. The database name is "basil" and the collection name is "july2020."
          img(src='/images/plants3.png' width='95%')

          h6 D3.js
          p
            s
              | First, I posted the moisture, temperature and humidity data in json format and used 
              u
                a(href='https://d3js.org/') d3.js
              |  to draw the line graphs.
          pre
            != codeSnippet4

          p Unfortunately, the volume of data posted slowed down this website after a week. In the end, I downloaded the data from MongoDB and uploaded it into 
            a(href='https://observablehq.com/' target='_blank') Observable
            |  to graph the data and embed the graph on this website.

